  Subtitle: A DWARF PLANET
  Paragraph: Counted as the ninth planet from 1930 until 2006, Pluto is now the best known of the dwarf planets. New Horizons flew past in 2015 and found mountains of water ice and a vast heart-shaped plain of frozen nitrogen that is still being resurfaced today.
